          %h2#BasicIdea Basic idea in category theory
          %p
            The general idea is that a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated from
            small data: from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+objects"} small objects
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+colimits"} small colimits
          %h3#generation_from_generators Generation from generators
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            is, at least roughly, an analogue for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            of the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated module
          #FinitelyGeneratedAbelianGroup.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated
              if there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota \colon S \hookrightarrow U(A)
            %p
              of the underlying set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(A)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a sum of such generating elements.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              We always have the maximal such presentation where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = U(A)
              is the whole underlying set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon F(U(A)) \to A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
              %em smaller
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is.
          %p
            Now, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of “commutative sum” is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a category with all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+colimits"} small colimits
          #GenerationOfCategoryFromSubcategoryUnderColimits.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              We say a subclass
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow Obj(\mathcal{C})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              or equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0 \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
              on this subclass
              %em generates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              if every object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of objects in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D \to \mathcal{C}^0 \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
                    \\,.
          %p
            As before, such a presentation is all the more useful the “smaller” the generating data is. In order to grasp the various aspects of the notion of “smallness” in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            we need to recall the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
          %h3#small_data Small data
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa = {\vert S\vert}
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular
              if every
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of sets of cardinality smaller than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              and indexed by a set of cardinality smaller than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is itself of cardinality smaller than
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The smallest
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              is
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℵ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0 = {\vert \mathbb{N}\vert}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
              is itself a finite set. (See the entry on
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
          %p
            We can now speak of objects that are “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            \-small sums” using the notion of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
              is one where every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of size
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt \kappa
              has a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              In an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℵ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
              every finite diagram has a cocone. This is equivalent to:
            %ol
              %li
                %p for every pair of objects there is a third object such that both have a morphism to it;
              %li
                %p
                  for every pair of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
                  there is a morphism out of their codomain such that the two composites are equal.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+diagram"} tower diagram
              category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N}, \leq)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_0 \to X_1 \to X_2 \to \cdots
            %p is filtered.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \gt \kappa
              a bigger
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
              is in particular also
              = succeed "-filtered." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p Using this we have the central definition now:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over a
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            A crucial characterizing property of
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          #FilteredColimitsAndFiniteLimits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A colimit in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+limits"} small limits
            %p
              In particular a colimit in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is filtered (meaning:
              = succeed "-filtered)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℵ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              if it commutes with
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon I \to \mathcal{C}
              any
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi i
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\to_i}{\lim} \mathcal{C}(A,X_i) \to \mathcal{C}(A, \underset{\to_i}{\lim} X_i)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              if it is
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %em some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \gt \kappa
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "-compact." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              commutes with the colimit over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              precisely if every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to \underset{\to_i}{\lim} X_i
              lifts to a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X_j
              into one of the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_j
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\cdots&amp;\to&amp;X_{j-1} &amp;\to&amp; X_j &amp;\to&amp; X_{j+1} &amp;\to&amp; \cdots
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;{}^{\mathllap{\exists \hat f}}\nearrow&amp;\downarrow &amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;A&amp; \stackrel{f}{\to} &amp; \underset{\to}{\lim} X_i
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is “small enough” such that mapping it into the sum of all the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              it always entirely lands inside one of the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              There is a close relation between the notion of “compact” as in, on the one hand,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topos"} compact topos
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              as above. This is mediated by proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredColimitsAndFiniteLimits"}
          %h3#locally_presentable_category_generated_from_colimits_over_small_objects Locally presentable category: generated from colimits over small objects
          %p Using this we can now say:
          #LocallyPresentableCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              if it has all small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              and there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow Obj(\mathcal{C})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+objects"} small objects
              such that this generates
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GenerationOfCategoryFromSubcategoryUnderColimits"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              The adjective “locally” in “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"}> locally presentable category
              ” is to indicate that the condition is all about the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
          %p There are a bunch of equivalent reformulations of the notion of locally presentable category. One of the more important ones we again motivate first by analogy with presentable modules:
          %h3#generation_exhibited_by_epimorphism_from_a_free_object Generation exhibited by epimorphism from a free object
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              If an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is generated by a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow U(A)
              as in example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FinitelyGeneratedAbelianGroup"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L \colon F(S) \to A
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(S)
              generated by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combination"} formal sums
              of elements in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(\sum_k s_k) \coloneqq \sum_k \iota(s_k)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
              of the notion
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              is the notion of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
              of a category
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(\mathcal{C}^0)
          %p Accordingly:
          .num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon \mathcal{C}^0 \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
              generates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              under colimits as in defn.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GenerationOfCategoryFromSubcategoryUnderColimits"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L \colon PSh(\mathcal{C}^0) \to \mathcal{C}
            %p
              which sends formal colimits to actual colimits in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi k
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(\underset{\to_k}{\lim} s_k) \coloneqq \underset{\to_k}{\lim} \iota(s_k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              by construction preserves all colimits.
          %p
            Therefore conversely, given a colimit-preserving functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon PSh(\mathcal{C}^0) \to \mathcal{C}
            we want to say that it
            %em locally presents
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is “suitably epi”.
          %p It turns out that “suitably epi” is to be the following:
          #Localization.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon PSh(\mathcal{C}^0) \to \mathcal{C}
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0
              is an
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  has a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon \mathcal{C} \to PSh(\mathcal{C}^0)
                  with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi R
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\circ R \simeq id_{\mathcal{C}}
              %li
                %p such that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                      is
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                      to
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi L
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi L
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ L
                      preserves
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi κ
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          %p
            With this notion we have the following analog of the familiar statement that an abelian group is generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            precisely if there is an epimorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
