          #AdamekRosickyTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is locally presentable according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyPresentableCategory"}
              precisely if it is an accessible localization, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Localization"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L \colon PSh(\mathcal{C}^0) \to \mathcal{C}
            %p
              for some small category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#AdamekRosicky"}> Adámek-Rosický, prop 1.46
            ).
          %h3#left_exact_localizations Left exact localizations
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon PSh(\mathcal{C}^0) \to \mathcal{C}
              from theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdamekRosickyTheorem"}
              in addition is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          %h2#summary Summary and overview
          %p
            In summary the discussion
            %a{:href => "#BasicIdea"} above
            says that the notion of locally presentable categories sits in a sequence of notions as indicated in the row labeled “category theory” in the following table. The other rows are supposed to indicate that regarding a category as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C1%29-category"} (1,1)-category
            and simply varying in this story the parameters
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
